think ALES87 opened the floor side with the hard center clipper but left a JUMP at the boundary (|x| = t+1 leaps to t+1). The DRIVE family already carries a hard/soft pair on the ceiling side (ALES78 hard clip, ALES79 soft clip); crux-first within tier, the cleanest next move is the floor-side soft form that rounds ALES87's corner — y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x − sign(x)·t, the survivor rising continuously from zero. This completes a hard/soft pair on BOTH sides.
think Chose the soft center clipper over the booked DC blocker for this lap: it is exact, memoryless, and low-risk (high confidence of GREEN), continuing the proven pattern, while the DC blocker's fractional feedback is a meatier round kept booked. Exactness holds by construction — a positive survivor lands in [1, sample_max], a negative in [sample_min, −1], the dead zone at 0 — so no saturate is owed; the magnitude is taken in i32 so |sample_min| = 32768 is representable.
think The teaching this rung adds is the soft/hard bond, proven sample for sample against ALES87: soft and hard center clip silence the SAME dead zone, and on every survivor |soft| = |hard| − t (the soft form exactly t quieter). The map is odd and — honestly — NOT idempotent (each pass subtracts t again; a shift, not a mask), stated plainly rather than dressed in a symmetry it lacks. The boundary law proves continuity (|x| = t → 0, |x| = t+1 → ±1) directly against ALES87's leap.
obs Followed the parametric-waveshaper pattern exactly (center_clip.rye / soft_drive.rye): module + design doc + witness + README status-line sync and re-stamp + session log, one signed commit. Eight laws proven; the witness imports ALES87 and re-proves the bond beside it. Witness GREEN on the first run; tame_style_check bans clean; width exit 0. The postcondition assert spells the exact map per sign, the @intCast guarded by a range assert.
loom witness=ales_soft_center_clip_witness selftest=GREEN laws=8 module_lines=196
